<%# An action value: what cannot be undone, the reason button's irreversible form under the setting: "Ordet…" always
    opens a box in the role alarm with what disappears, the action's button with Avbryt and, under them, the reason
    when the place asks for one. The reason and the button belong, by HTML's form attribute, to the action's own hidden
    form, drawn after the page's form (_action_forms), so that nothing nests and the page's own fields are never sent
    with it. Emptying the previews says how many addresses go (every row it removes: cards, queued and failed) and
    how much of the picture folder; any other action says its confirmation. A route that is missing draws nothing; a row that cannot be chosen draws the label quietly. %>
<% url = gk_gui_stuff_action_url(value) %>
<% if url %>
  <div class="gk-gui-stuff-form-page-value">
    <% if disabled %>
      <span class="gk-gui-stuff-form-page-quiet"><%= value.label %></span>
    <% else %>
      <% form_id = gk_gui_stuff_action_form_id(row, value) %>
      <% (@gk_gui_stuff_actions ||= []) << [form_id, url] %>
      <% question = nil
         info = value.confirm.presence
         if row.key == GkGuiStuffExternalPreviewController::ROW_KEY && value.name == 'clear' && defined?(GkGuiStuff::External::Storage)
           begin
             rows = ::GkGuiStuffLinkPreview.count
             bytes = GkGuiStuff::External::Storage.ours.sum { |p| File.file?(p) ? File.size(p) : 0 }
             question = l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_lpe_clear_question)
             info = l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_lpe_clear_what, count: rows, size: number_to_human_size(bytes))
           rescue StandardError
             question = nil
           end
         end %>
      <%= gk_gui_stuff_reason_button(value.label, reason: GkGuiStuffAppearanceController::PLACE, irreversible: true, question: question, info: info,
                                     form: form_id, html: { form: form_id }) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
